Clodronic acid disodium salt is an organic compound of phosphorus. It is a phosphonic acid derivative, so heading 2931 (other organo-inorganic compounds) is the likely home. Heading 2931 covers organo-phosphorus compounds, and clodronic acid is (dichloromethylene)bisphosphonic acid, which has a P-C bond.

Alternatively, if it is put up as a medicament in dosage form it would fall in 3004, but this is the bulk active ingredient, so 2931 applies. The HTSUS 2931 subheadings are 2931.10 through 2931.90. In recent versions, 2931.90 is "Other", with statistical suffixes such as 2931.90.9050 (other) and 2931.90.9045 or similar for specific items. I recall 2931.90.90 as "Other," with the 10-digit codes 2931.90.9010 for a specific compound and 2931.90.9050 for other. Newer revisions split the subheadings, using 2931.41 to 2931.49 for specific compounds and 2931.90 for others. Clodronic acid is not specifically named, so I settle on 2931.90.9050 (the exact suffix is not certain).

{"hts_code": "2931.90.9050", "reason": "Clodronate disodium is a bulk organo-phosphorus (bisphosphonate, P-C bond) compound not specifically named elsewhere, so it falls in heading 2931 under the 'other' organo-inorganic compounds subheading."}
